From 3f33dd35e09bb6b155d8576563d6053aa4b898c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 09:59:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm: move pending pageflips to the crtc

pending pageflips need to live in the crtc so a modeset/disconnect can
actually abort a pageflip coming or rather return if it the event
arrives. previously we also UAF on hotplugging meanwhile a pageflip was pending.
so we now use a global static to the backend, lookup pending pageflips by crtcid
and ignore stale ones. because the kernel from what i can tell does not abort a pageflip on a
disconnected crtc so the event still comes.

we also dont want to send double presented on tearing, add a ASYNC guard
in handlePF.

this should now guard against unwanted pageflips from crtcs, gone,
reconnected with same crtc ids, pageflips arriving when it shouldnt
because broken drivers etc.
